BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Getting Wiggly with Composting with OC Waste and Recycling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T100000
DTSTAMP:20260618T115420Z
UID:d11bf064b72a211cf7aa13c38edfb15f@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nThis summer\, Pretend City Children
 &#8217\;s Museum teamed up with OC Waste &amp\; Recycling to bring hands-o
 n vermicomposting education to young learners! ♻️🪱🌱 Through in
 teractive presentations and activities\, kids explore how worms help recyc
 le food scraps into nutrient-rich compost\, learning firsthand how small a
 ctions can make a big impact for our planet! Together\, we’re making org
 anics recycling fun\, engaging\, and accessible for the next generation of
  environmental stewards. \nTime: 10 am  \nIncluded with museum admissio
 n \nActivities take place throughout the day while supplies last. \n*Eve
 nts and times are subject to change.\nAbout the play partner: OC Waste &a
 mp\; Recycling serves the County’s solid waste disposal needs by provid
 ing waste management services\, operating public landfills\, protecting t
 he local environment\, investing in renewable energy enterprises and pro
 moting recycling in order to ensure a safe and healthy community for cur
 rent and future generations. OCWR also provides education\, outreach\, and
  sustainability programs that help residents reduce waste and support stat
 e and local mandates. \n \nFrequently Asked Questions \nWhat is Gettin
 g Wiggly with Composting program? \nGetting Wiggly with Composting is a
  hands-on environmental learning experience at Pretend City Children’s M
 useum in Irvine\, California\, where children discover how worms turn food
  scraps into nutrient-rich compost through vermicomposting. \nIs this act
 ivity included with admission?\nYes. The vermicomposting activities are 
 included with regular museum admission. \nWhat ages is this program best 
 for?\nThe experience is designed for children ages 3–12 and their famili
 es. \nWill kids see real worms?\nYes. Children can learn about real worms
  and how they help break down food scraps into compost. \nAre there oth
 er days to attend this program?\nYes. The vermicomposting activities will 
 take place on June 6\, June 16\, June 23\, and June 30 from 10 am – 2 p
 m while supplies last.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events
 /getting-wiggly-with-composting-with-oc-waste-and-recycling/2026-06-23/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/getting-wiggly-with-composting-with
 -oc-waste-and-recycling/2026-06-23/
